tural products using HDPE resin | The company's key markets include residential, commercial, marine and industrial applications"}},"holding":{"sponsor":"Platinum Equity","status":"current","status_note":"Acquired July 2026 from a financial sponsor (agreement June 2026, closed 31 July 2026)","asset_class":"Private equity","deal_type":"Secondary buyout","value_creation_plan":"Platinum sees meaningful opportunities to expand Tangent's core offerings while continuing to innovate, and to bring its M&A and operational capabilities to bear to support the company's next phase of growth, including pursuing strategic add-on acquisitions.","value_creation_source_url":"https://www.platinumequity.com/news/platinum-equity-to-acquire-tangent-technologies/","notes":"Platinum portfolio status Active; seller not named."}},{"name":"PlayMetrics","website":"https://home.playmetrics.com/","description":"Leading provider of operations management software for youth sports organizations, purpose-built to simplify running a club, league, tournament or governing body with unified financial, operational, coaching and communication tools.","sector":"Software","subsector":"Youth sports management software","country":"United States","founded_year":2017,"business_model":"B2B SaaS (with integrated payments)","email":"support@playmetrics.com","email_type":"generic","leaders":[{"role":"ceo","name":"Mike Doernberg","title":"CEO & Founder","source_url":"https://home.playmetrics.com/about-playmetrics","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Our leadership team | Mike Doernberg | CEO & FOUNDER"},{"role":"coo","name":"Chris Smith","title":"COO","source_url":"https://home.playmetrics.com/about-playmetrics","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Chris Smith | COO | Chris has extensive experience as a financial and operating executive for growth companies, most recently as CFO/COO of ReverbNation"}],"notes":"PlayMetrics, LLC; 'proudly built in North Carolina' (Raleigh dateline in the merger release). In June 2025 Genstar acquired PlayMetrics from Blue Star Innovation Partners (and PSG) and merged it with Stack Sports (Dallas); Genstar is majority owner of the combined company and Michael Doernberg leads it as CEO. Serves over 2,700 youth sports organizations (June 2025). No revenue or headcount disclosed.","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://www.gencap.com/companies/","name":"Genstar Capital","kind":"sponsor","as_of":null,"evidence":"PlayMetrics is a leading provider of operations management software for youth sports organizations. PlayMetrics is purpose-built to simplify the unique complexities of running a club, league, tournament, or governing body"},"founded_year":{"url":"https://psgequity.com/news/blue-star-innovation-partners-and-psg-complete-sale-of-playmetrics-to-genstar-capital","name":"PSG","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2025-06-11","evidence":"Founded in 2017, PlayMetrics centralizes administrative functions for youth club sports organizations."},"country":{"url":"https://home.playmetrics.com/about-playmetrics","name":"PlayMetrics","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"Proudly built in North Carolina, PlayMetrics helps youth sports organizations conquer the chaos of their daily operations"},"email":{"url":"https://home.playmetrics.com/","name":"PlayMetrics","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"Help Center | support@playmetrics.com"},"business_model":{"url":"https://psgequity.com/news/blue-star-innovation-partners-and-psg-complete-sale-of-playmetrics-to-genstar-capital","name":"PSG","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2025-06-11","evidence":"On a single, user-friendly interface, PlayMetrics streamlines registration, scheduling, communication, payments, and coaching tools. ... expanding its customer base by 5x and optimizing its payments monetization strategy."},"sector":{"url":"https://www.gencap.com/companies/","name":"Genstar Capital","kind":"sponsor","as_of":null,"evidence":"Status: Current / 2025 Investment | Sector: Software | Genstar Team: Eli Weiss, Terry McKenna"}},"holding":{"sponsor":"Genstar Capital","status":"current","status_note":"Acquired from Blue Star Innovation Partners in June 2025 and merged with Stack Sports; Genstar is majority owner of the combined company","asset_class":"Private equity","deal_type":"Secondary buyout","value_creation_plan":"Genstar supported combining PlayMetrics with Stack Sports to create one of the largest sports technology platforms delivering comprehensive solutions to clubs, leagues, tournaments, state associations and governing bodies.","value_creation_source_url":"https://www.gencap.com/playmetrics-and-stack-sports-combine-to-create-leader-in-sports-software/","notes":"Genstar lists Status: Current / 2025 Investment, Sector: Software."}},{"name":"iBase-t","website":"https://www.ibaset.com/","description":"Leading provider of Manufacturing Operations Management software for aerospace and defense manufacturers and other complex industries, whose cloud-native Solumina platform covers manufacturing, quality and MRO operations.","sector":"Technology (Software)","subsector":"Manufacturing operations management (MES/MRO) software for aerospace and defense","country":"United States","founded_year":1986,"business_model":"B2B SaaS (subscription)","email":"inquiry@iBase-t.com","email_type":"generic","leaders":[{"role":"ceo","name":"Naveen Poonian","title":"Chief Executive Officer","source_url":"https://www.ibaset.com/leadership/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Naveen Poonian | Chief Executive Officer | Naveen Poonian is Chief Executive Officer of iBase-t"},{"role":"cfo","name":"Charlie Velasquez","title":"Chief Financial Officer","source_url":"https://www.ibaset.com/leadership/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Charlie Velasquez | Chief Financial Officer | Charlie is a seasoned Strategic Finance and Operations Executive"},{"role":"coo","name":"Scott Baril","title":"Chief Operating Officer","source_url":"https://www.ibaset.com/leadership/","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Scott Baril | Chief Operating Officer | As Chief Operating Officer, Scott leads the iBase-t Professional Services, Customer Success, Knowledge Services, and Product D[evelopment]"}],"notes":"Headquarters 26812 Vista Terrace, Lake Forest, CA 92630; offices in France (Blagnac), UK (Birmingham) and India (Ahmedabad). Customers include Lockheed Martin, Northrop Grumman, GE Aerospace, Rolls Royce, Pratt & Whitney and Textron. TA's strategic growth investment was announced 31 March 2026; TA's release thanks 'the Poonian family and the entire iBase-t team' for choosing TA; terms and stake size not disclosed. No revenue or headcount disclosed.","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://www.ta.com/portfolio/investments/ibase-t/","name":"TA Associates","kind":"sponsor","as_of":null,"evidence":"iBase-t is a leading provider of Manufacturing Operations Management software for aerospace and defense manufacturers, and other complex industries."},"founded_year":{"url":"https://www.ibaset.com/about-us/","name":"iBase-t","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"1986 | iBase-t opens its doors"},"country":{"url":"https://www.ibaset.com/contact/","name":"iBase-t","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"Headquarters | 26812 Vista Terrace | Lake Forest, CA 92630"},"email":{"url":"https://www.ibaset.com/contact/","name":"iBase-t","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"+33 5 34 50 91 70 | inquiry@iBase-t.com"},"business_model":{"url":"https://www.ibaset.com/leadership/","name":"iBase-t","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"As Chief Revenue Officer, Sebastian is responsible for expanding the company's SaaS subscription-based repeatable revenue mo[del]"},"sector":{"url":"https://www.ta.com/portfolio/investments/ibase-t/","name":"TA Associates","kind":"sponsor","as_of":null,"evidence":"Sector | Technology | Software | Investment Year | 2026 | Status | Current | Headquarters | Lake Forest, CA"}},"holding":{"sponsor":"TA Associates","status":"current","status_note":"Strategic growth investment announced March 2026","asset_class":"Private equity","deal_type":"Growth investment","value_creation_plan":"TA will partner with the iBase-t team as they accelerate product development, enhance go-to-market effectiveness and expand the company's leadership in digital manufacturing and sustainment solutions; the investment supports continued product innovation, AI capabilities and global expansion.","value_creation_source_url":"https://www.ta.com/news/ibase-t-announces-strategic-growth-investment-from-ta-to-accelerate-ai-powered-digital-manufacturing-and-mro-transformation-in-aerospace-defense/","notes":"TA team: Ashutosh Agrawal, Maria Jose Arrea, Nik Cable, Yana Kaplun, Nicholas D. Leppla. Stake size not disclosed."}},{"name":"Stay22","website":"https://www.stay22.com","description":"Content monetization company that helps creators, publishers and brands convert audience intent into revenue, using AI-driven decisioning to route users to relevant online travel agencies and retailers.","sector":"Technology","subsector":"Creator and publisher affiliate monetization platform (travel and retail)","country":"Canada","business_model":"B2B2C affiliate/commission platform for creators, publishers and event organizers","email":"support@stay22.com","email_type":"generic","leaders":[{"role":"ceo","name":"Andrew Lockhead","title":"CEO and Co-Founder","source_url":"https://www.summitpartners.com/news/stay22-raises-122m-summit-partners","source_kind":"sponsor","evidence":"said Andrew Lockhead, CEO and Co-Founder of Stay22."},{"role":"other","name":"Hamed Al-Khabbaz","title":"CTO & Co-Founder","source_url":"https://www.stay22.com/about-us","source_kind":"company","evidence":"Stay22 came to be when CTO & Co-Founder Hamed Al-Khabbaz struggled to find a hotel for an e-sports event in Germany."}],"notes":"Founded and headquartered in Montreal. Summit Partners made a USD 122 million minority growth investment (announced 26 February 2026). Stay22 processed more than USD 1 billion in annual transactions in 2025 and its retail vertical delivered USD 80 million GMV in 2025; these are transaction volumes, not company revenue, so revenue is left blank. Headcount more than tripled over the two years to February 2026 (no absolute number). More than 5,500 creators use the platform.","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://www.summitpartners.com/companies/stay22","name":"Summit Partners","kind":"sponsor","as_of":null,"evidence":"Stay22 is a content monetization company that helps creators, publishers and brands convert audience intent into revenue. Powered by AI-driven decisioning, the Stay22 platform analyzes real-time contextual and behavioral signals to route users to relevant online travel agencies and retailers"},"country":{"url":"https://www.summitpartners.com/news/stay22-raises-122m-summit-partners","name":"Summit Partners","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-02-26","evidence":"Founded and headquartered in Montreal, Stay22 is an intelligent, data-driven technology platform"},"email":{"url":"https://www.stay22.com/contact-us","name":"Stay22","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"reach out to support@stay22.com and we'd be happy to help!"},"business_model":{"url":"https://www.summitpartners.com/news/stay22-raises-122m-summit-partners","name":"Summit Partners","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-02-26","evidence":"Today, more than 5,500 creators use Stay22 to identify high-value affiliate opportunities that help turn content into revenue."},"sector":{"url":"https://www.summitpartners.com/companies/stay22","name":"Summit Partners","kind":"sponsor","as_of":null,"evidence":"Content monetization platform | Invested in | 2026 | Status | Current | Location | Montreal, CA | Sector | Technology"}},"holding":{"sponsor":"Summit Partners","status":"current","status_note":"USD 122 million minority growth investment, February 2026","asset_class":"Growth equity","deal_type":"Minority stake","value_creation_plan":"The funding will support Stay22's continued global expansion, product innovation, team growth and investment in its partner ecosystem; Stay22 plans to expand beyond travel into broader creator monetization across retail verticals (food, fashion, DIY, lifestyle, consumer technology).","value_creation_source_url":"https://www.summitpartners.com/news/stay22-raises-122m-summit-partners","notes":"Summit's Colin Mistele and Daniel Kim joined the board."}},{"name":"Corgi","website":"https://www.corgi.insure","description":"Licensed, AI-native commercial insurance carrier that owns the full stack across underwriting, claims and policy administration, built for startups and technology companies.","sector":"Fintech & Payments","subsector":"AI-native commercial insurance carrier (insurtech)","country":"United States","founded_year":2024,"business_model":"B2B (commercial insurance carrier, direct and embedded distribution)","email":"hello@corgi.insure","email_type":"generic","leaders":[{"role":"ceo","name":"Nico Laqua","title":"Co-founder and CEO","source_url":"https://www.corgi.insure/press-releases/series-b","source_kind":"company","evidence":"said Nico Laqua, co-founder and CEO of Corgi."},{"role":"coo","name":"Emily Yuan","title":"Co-founder and COO","source_url":"https://www.corgi.insure/press-releases/series-b","source_kind":"company","evidence":"said Emily Yuan, co-founder and COO of Corgi."}],"notes":"San Francisco, CA. Raised a $160 million Series B at a $1.3 billion valuation led by TCV (7 May 2026) and a $106 million Series B1 led by TCV at a $2.6 billion valuation (28 May 2026); total funding $378 million per the company. Coverage may be underwritten through Corgi Insurance Company, Inc. (admitted P&C carrier) and partner carriers; Corgi Insurance Services, Inc. holds producer licences (CA License #6012791). The company says it was profitable in April 2026 but discloses no revenue figures.","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://www.tcv.com/partnerships/corgi","name":"TCV","kind":"sponsor","as_of":null,"evidence":"Corgi is a licensed, AI-native commercial insurance carrier that owns the full stack across underwriting, claims, and policy administration."},"founded_year":{"url":"https://www.tcv.com/partnerships/corgi","name":"TCV","kind":"sponsor","as_of":null,"evidence":"Location | San Francisco, CA | Founded in | 2024 | Focus Area | Fintech & Payments"},"country":{"url":"https://www.tcv.com/partnerships/corgi","name":"TCV","kind":"sponsor","as_of":null,"evidence":"Location | San Francisco, CA"},"email":{"url":"https://www.corgi.insure/about","name":"Corgi","kind":"company","as_of":null,"evidence":"hello@corgi.insure Email LinkedIn X"},"business_model":{"url":"https://www.tcv.com/partnerships/corgi","name":"TCV","kind":"sponsor","as_of":null,"evidence":"to deliver faster policy quoting, flexible product design, and an improved experience for embedded distribution partners and end-customers."},"sector":{"url":"https://www.tcv.com/partnerships/corgi","name":"TCV","kind":"sponsor","as_of":null,"evidence":"Focus Area | Fintech & Payments | Status | Active"}},"holding":{"sponsor":"TCV","status":"current","status_note":"Led the $160M Series B (May 2026) and the $106M Series B1 (May 2026)","asset_class":"Growth equity","deal_type":"Venture round","value_creation_plan":"The Series B funding supports continued expansion of Corgi's startup insurance products, including broader coverage, deeper distribution and ongoing investment in the AI systems that power underwriting, claims and policy operations, and a move into new verticals beginning with trucking.","value_creation_source_url":"https://www.corgi.insure/press-releases/series-b","notes":"TCV portfolio status Active. Plan is the company's statement of the use of funds; TCV did not publish its own plan on the pages read."}}]$pp$::jsonb);
